# This file is the most consequential file in the repository.
#
# The model weights are about 20 GB, and about 40 GB on disk before the
# duplicate copy is reclaimed. Without the rules below, a single
# "git add -A" tries to commit all of it. GitHub rejects that, and the
# attempt leaves a broken repository folder behind.
#
# Every rule has a comment saying what it catches and why.
# A line that starts with "#" is a comment. A line that starts with "/"
# matches only at the top level of this repository.

# --- model weights: NEVER commit (20-40 GB) ---

# The model folder this repository downloads by default.
/Qwen3.8-*/

# Other Qwen folders converted for MLX, whatever version number they carry.
/Qwen*-MLX-*/

# Belt and braces: any top-level folder with MLX or GGUF in its name is a
# model folder. Both strings appear only in model folder names in practice.
#
# Spelled out letter by letter because git matches these case-sensitively
# whenever core.ignorecase is false — which is the case on a case-sensitive
# disk and in most Linux build machines. The community publishes folders named
# "...-mlx-4bit" in lower case, and /*MLX*/ alone does not catch those.
/*[Mm][Ll][Xx]*/
/*[Gg][Gg][Uu][Ff]*/

# The conventional folder people use when they keep several models.
/models/

# git-lfs storage. It normally lives inside .git, but a mis-set GIT_LFS_PATH or
# an interrupted download can create it here instead. It holds a full second
# copy of the weights, so it is as large as the model folder itself.
/lfs/

# The file format MLX model weights ship in. This glob is the safety net:
# it catches a model downloaded into a folder name the rules above miss.
*.safetensors

# The file format llama.cpp model weights ship in. Same safety net.
*.gguf

# Older single-file weight formats. Still common on model download pages.
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth
*.npz
*.mlx

# The other large files a model folder carries. These are not weights, so none
# of the rules above catch them, and a model downloaded into a folder name the
# rules above do not anticipate would otherwise stage about 22 MB of them.
# Measured in this checkpoint: tokenizer.json 12.2 MB, vocab.json 6.4 MB,
# merges.txt 3.2 MB, model.safetensors.index.json 207 KB.
tokenizer.json
tokenizer_config.json
vocab.json
merges.txt
model.safetensors.index.json
chat_template.jinja

# --- python ---

# The optional Python virtual environment. It is a few hundred MB, it is
# rebuilt in one command, and it contains machine-specific absolute paths
# that break on anyone else's Mac.
.venv/
venv/

# Compiled Python files. Generated on every run, never worth committing.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- logs and runtime state ---

# Server logs. They can grow to hundreds of MB and they may quote the text
# of your own prompts.
logs/
*.log

# The mlx-serve working folder: its cached prompt data and its own logs.
# The cached data alone can reach 10 GB.
.mlx-serve/

# Output from the benchmark script.
bench-out/

# --- local config (may contain an API_KEY) ---

# Your own copy of config.env.example. It can hold a secret key, so it must
# never leave your Mac. The example file IS committed; this one is not.
config.env
.env
.env.local

# --- macOS / editors ---

# The hidden file macOS writes into every folder you open in Finder.
.DS_Store

# Editor settings. Personal, not project settings.
.idea/
.vscode/
